{{also|Áustria|Àustria}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:AU-map-en.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.09|Map of Austria]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|Austria}}, a Latinization of {{der|en|goh|Ōstarrīhhi}} (the first element of which means "east" and stems from {{der|en|gem-pro|*austraz||eastern}}, and the second element of which is {{m|goh|rīhhi||realm}}. See {{m|en|east}}, {{m|en|eastern}} for more.

Distantly cognate to {{m|en|Australia}}: it derives from the same Proto-Indo-European root, but via Latin, where it came to mean “south” rather than “east”. Compare also {{m|en|Austrasia}}.

